{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And the fugitive came.</b> According to its plain sense, this is Og, who escaped from the battle. And so it is written: ״כִּי רַק עוֹג נִשְׁאַר מִיֶּתֶר הָרְפָאִים״ (Deuteronomy 3) — and this is נִשְׁאַר: that Amraphel and his companions did not kill him when they struck the Rephaim at Ashteroth-karnaim. This is its midrash — Bereshit Rabbah: this is Og, who escaped from the generation of the Flood; and this is מִיֶּתֶר הָרְפָאִים, as it is said ״הַנְּפִילִים הָיוּ בָאָרֶץ״ וגו׳ (above, 6) — and he intended that Abram be killed so he could take Sarah." "<b>The Hebrew.</b> Who came from across the river (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Abram's allies.</b> Who cut a covenant with him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:39.417422253Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}